{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011Cf5mc4SMtLJahDyYmy7gJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Repository findings (search results):**\n- `Order.kt:11` — Order entity lacks status field\n- `OrderController.kt:17` — OrderController has create, getById, list; no cancel endpoint\n- `OrderRepository.kt:10` — InMemoryOrderRepository stores orders in ConcurrentHashMap\n- `Shipment.kt:9,23` — Shipment has ShipmentStatus enum with CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED\n- `ShipmentRepository.kt:10` — Needs method to find shipments by orderId\n- `ShipmentController.kt:26` — Creates shipments without checking order status\n- `ApiExceptions.kt:18,22` — ResourceNotFoundException (404), ConflictException (409) already defined\n- `ApiError.kt:31` — ErrorCode enum with ORDER_NOT_FOUND, ORDER_ALREADY_EXISTS, SHIPMENT_* codes\n\n**Conventions this repository has:**\n- All errors throw `ApiException` subclasses; `GlobalExceptionHandler` converts them to `ApiError` envelope\n- Controllers never assemble error bodies; they throw exceptions (see OrderController:23-27)\n- Tests verify both HTTP status and error envelope body (see OrderControllerTest:62-74)\n- Repositories are in-memory with `ConcurrentHashMap` and include `clear()` for test reset\n- New entities get `data class` with immutable fields (see Order:11, Shipment:9)\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `Order.kt` — Must add `status` field; new orders default to `ACTIVE`\n2. `OrderController.kt` — Must add `POST /{orderId}/cancel` endpoint\n3. `ApiError.kt` — Must add error codes for shipment confirmation conflict\n4. `ShipmentRepository.kt` — Must add method to find shipments by orderId\n5. `ShipmentController.kt` — Must reject shipment creation for `CANCELLED` orders\n6. `OrderControllerTest.kt` — Must add tests for cancel endpoint and its five cases\n7. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — Must add test that shipment creation fails for cancelled orders\n\n**Risks:**\n- Adding status field to immutable `Order` data class will break all callers that construct it; must update Order construction in create endpoint\n- Cancellation must be all-or-nothing: if *any* shipment is CONFIRMED, reject and rollback (no state change)\n- Must prevent creating shipments against non-existent orders (current behavior must be preserved per requirement)\n- Error codes need to be added to enum without breaking serialization\n\n**Open questions:**\n- Should I add a new error code like `ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENTS` or reuse existing codes? The requirement says \"Error responses are consistent with the rest of this API\" — let me check if there are similar conflict scenarios in the existing tests.\n\nLooking at the tests, conflicts use 409 status. The requirement says \"rejected with HTTP 409\" for confirmed shipments. I'll add error codes that make the conflict reason clear.\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **Order.kt** — Add enum `OrderStatus` with `ACTIVE` and `CANCELLED`; add `status: OrderStatus` field to `Order` data class. New orders created will have `status = ACTIVE`.\n\n2. **OrderController.kt** — Inject `ShipmentRepository` in addition to `OrderRepository`. In the `create` endpoint, set status to `ACTIVE` when constructing Order. Add new `POST /{orderId}/cancel` endpoint that:\n   - Finds order or throws `ResourceNotFoundException` (404)\n   - If order is already `CANCELLED`, return it unchanged (idempotent)\n   - Fetch all shipments for that order from ShipmentRepository\n   - If any shipment has status `CONFIRMED`, throw `ConflictException` (409) and make no changes\n   - Otherwise, update each `CREATED` shipment to `CANCELLED` and update order to `CANCELLED`\n   - Return the cancelled order with 200 OK\n\n3. **ApiError.kt** — Add error codes: `ORDER_CANCELLED` (when trying to create shipment for cancelled order) and `ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENTS` (when trying to cancel order with confirmed shipments).\n\n4. **ShipmentRepository.kt** — Add method `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` that filters the store by orderId.\n\n5. **ShipmentController.kt** — In the `create` endpoint, after checking if shipment exists, inject `OrderRepository`, fetch the order, and check if it's cancelled. If cancelled, throw `ConflictException` with code `ORDER_CANCELLED`. If order doesn't exist, allow creation (requirement says \"keeps its current behaviour\").\n\n6. **OrderControllerTest.kt** — Add five new test cases:\n   - Cancelling an active order succeeds and returns cancelled order\n   - Cancelling updates CREATED shipments to CANCELLED\n   - Cancelling an already-cancelled order succeeds with no change (idempotent)\n   - Cancelling fails with 409 if order has a CONFIRMED shipment (and nothing changes)\n   - Cancelling non-existent order fails with 404\n\n7. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Add one test: Creating a shipment for a cancelled order fails with 409 and includes the error envelope.\n\n**Alternative rejected and why:**\n- I considered making Order a mutable entity with a setStatus() method, but the existing codebase uses immutable data classes throughout, which is the Kotlin/Spring idiom. Adding mutability would break convention.\n- I considered handling shipment cancellation in a separate service layer, but the requirement doesn't mention one and it's small enough to keep in the controller.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n*Cancelling an active order:*\n1. Client: `POST /orders/O-1/cancel`\n2. OrderController.cancel(): fetch order from OrderRepository\n3. If not found → throw `ResourceNotFoundException(ORDER_NOT_FOUND, \"...\")` → GlobalExceptionHandler → 404 with error envelope\n4. If already CANCELLED → return it unchanged (200 OK with Order body)\n5. If ACTIVE:\n   a. Fetch all shipments via ShipmentRepository.findByOrderId(O-1)\n   b. Check if any has status CONFIRMED\n   c. If yes → throw `ConflictException(ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENTS, \"...\")` → 409 with error envelope (NO STATE CHANGE)\n   d. If no → for each shipment with status CREATED, call repository.save() to update to CANCELLED\n   e. Save order with status CANCELLED\n   f. Return order (200 OK with Order body)\n\n*Creating a shipment for a cancelled order:*\n1. Client: `POST /shipments` with orderId = O-1\n2. ShipmentController.create(): check if shipment ID exists (reject if yes)\n3. Fetch order from OrderRepository\n4. If order exists and status is CANCELLED → throw `ConflictException(ORDER_CANCELLED, \"...\")` → 409\n5. Otherwise proceed to save (current behavior preserved for non-existent orders)\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. `OrderControllerTest.cancelsActiveOrder()` — Create order O-1 (ACTIVE), cancel it, verify status is CANCELLED in response\n2. `OrderControllerTest.cancelUpdatesCreatedShipments()` — Create order O-1, create CREATED shipment S-1 for it, cancel order, verify S-1 is now CANCELLED\n3. `OrderControllerTest.cancelAlreadyCancelledOrderIsIdempotent()` — Create order O-1, cancel it, cancel again, verify second cancel succeeds with no error\n4. `OrderControllerTest.cancelFailsIfConfirmedShipmentExists()` — Create order O-1, create CREATED shipment S-1 and manually set it to CONFIRMED (via repository), try to cancel, verify 409 error code ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENTS, verify order is still ACTIVE and shipment still CONFIRMED\n5. `OrderControllerTest.cancelNonExistentOrderFails()` — Try to cancel O-999, verify 404 with ORDER_NOT_FOUND\n6. `ShipmentControllerTest.createShipmentForCancelledOrderFails()` — Create and cancel order O-1, try to create shipment for O-1, verify 409 with ORDER_CANCELLED\n\n**Acceptance criteria mapping (preliminary):**\n1. Existing build passes ← Will run `mvnw test` at end\n2. Existing tests pass ← Will verify existing tests still pass\n3. POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel cancels active order, persists it, cancels CREATED shipments ← Test #1, #2\n4. Error responses consistent ← Using existing ApiException pattern, new codes in ErrorCode enum\n5. Repeated cancel succeeds; confirmed shipment blocks with no change; unknown order 404; no shipment for cancelled order ← Tests #3, #4, #5, #6\n6. No new Maven dependency ← Won't touch pom.xml\n7. No unrelated production file changes ← Only touch Order, OrderController, OrderRepository, ShipmentRepository, ShipmentController, ApiError\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2458,"cache_read_input_tokens":19433,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2458},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a3c58f54-859a-4ae8-a87b-0122513b12c7","uuid":"836ab1d0-a6f8-4aec-aeaa-e904f227fd37","timestamp":"2026-09-15T19:23:17.162Z","request_id":"req_011Cf5mc3fUbUQ7uHfMBKLPq"}
