d 1 new test case for cancelled order rejection. Required because ticket demands test coverage.\n\n**Unresolved findings:** None. All acceptance criteria are addressed in code or tests.\n\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n\n```\nRequirement   Add POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint with order status tracking (ACTIVE/CANCELLED), preventing shipment creation for cancelled orders, and blocking cancellation when confirmed shipments exist.\n\nChanged       Order.kt — added OrderStatus enum and status field to Order entity\n              OrderController.kt — injected ShipmentRepository, updated create() to set ACTIVE status, added cancel() endpoint with all-or-nothing semantics\n              ApiError.kt — added ORDER_CANCELLED and ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENTS error codes\n              ShipmentRepository.kt — added findByOrderId() method to fetch shipments for an order\n              ShipmentController.kt — injected OrderRepository, added check to reject shipment creation for cancelled orders\n              OrderControllerTest.kt — added 5 tests for cancel endpoint (active order, shipment cancellation, idempotency, confirmed shipment conflict, non-existent order)\n              ShipmentControllerTest.kt — added 1 test for shipment rejection on cancelled order\n\nTests         OrderControllerTest.cancels an active order and returns it with CANCELLED status — verifies cancel endpoint works on ACTIVE orders\n              OrderControllerTest.cancel updates CREATED shipments to CANCELLED — verifies cascading status change to shipments\n              OrderControllerTest.cancelling an already cancelled order succeeds and changes nothing — verifies idempotent retry behavior\n              OrderControllerTest.cancel fails with 409 if order has a CONFIRMED shipment and changes nothing — verifies all-or-nothing semantics and no state change on conflict\n              OrderControllerTest.cancelling a non-existent order returns 404 — verifies 404 for missing orders\n              ShipmentControllerTest.rejects creating a shipment for a cancelled order with 409 — verifies shipments cannot be created for cancelled orders\n\nVerification  Command: ./mvnw test from sample-service/\n              Result: BUILD SUCCESS, 19 tests run (9 OrderControllerTest, 6 ShipmentControllerTest, 1 SampleServiceApplicationTests, 3 CustomerControllerTest), 0 failures\n\nNot done      None — all acceptance criteria met, all tests passing, no forbidden files modified\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3159,"cache_read_input_tokens":35771,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3159},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a3c58f54-859a-4ae8-a87b-0122513b12c7","uuid":"3a921a74-dd2c-4521-8646-8f3f2d7a1c8b","timestamp":"2026-09-15T19:25:09.025Z","request_id":"req_011Cf5mmLPYyhxYdec2ENryH"}
